# The errors each cmdlet raises, and those each class's methods throw,
# written by hand. tools/Export-Reference.ps1 writes each under an Errors
# heading: a cmdlet's on its powershell/<Group>-Cmdlets.md entry, a class's
# on its Types.md entry. It stops when a cmdlet has no list, when a list
# names a cmdlet or a class the module does not export, or when a list
# names an id src/ does not raise.
@{
    Cmdlets = @{
        'Clear-WgpuBuffer' = '`WgpuNoBuffer`, `WgpuOutOfRange`, `WgpuClear`, `WgpuSubmit`, `WgpuSubmitThread`, `WgpuWrite`, `WgpuPoll` and `WgpuStopped`; and for a buffer whose bytes do not fill whole 4-byte words, whose last word is read back first, `WgpuRead` and `WgpuMap`. Each is described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md), as is PWRS''s `PwrsConversionError` for a `-Value` that does not convert to a number.'
        'Close-WgpuDevice' = '`WgpuNoDevice`, without `-Device` when no default device is open, and from waiting for the work already given to the device, `WgpuPoll` and `WgpuStopped`; each described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md).'
        'Compare-WgpuTexture' = '`WgpuNoTexture`; `WgpuCompare`, for textures of another dimension, size or number of layers, and for a `-Channel` the textures do not both store; and `WgpuSsim`, from SSIM''s pass. From reading the textures back, `WgpuTextureUsage`, `WgpuAspect`, `WgpuBufferTooLarge`, `WgpuBuffer`, `WgpuTextureRead`, `WgpuSubmit`, `WgpuSubmitThread`, `WgpuPoll`, `WgpuRead`, `WgpuMap` and `WgpuStopped`; from decoding their texels, `WgpuTextureDecode` and `WgpuTexels`; and with `-Difference`, from making the picture, `WgpuTexture`, `WgpuTexelCount` and `WgpuTextureWrite`. Each is described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md).'
        'Convert-WgpuTexture' ='`WgpuNoTexture`, `WgpuRotate`, `WgpuTransform`, `WgpuSwizzle`, `WgpuGrayscale`, `WgpuAdjust` and `WgpuColorSpace`; `WgpuNormalMap`, for a normal step on a format without the channel it writes, and `-NormalMips` with the Min or Max filter; `WgpuBlur`, `WgpuSharpen`, `WgpuEdges` and `WgpuFilterEdge`, for a filter setting out of range or given without its filter, and `WgpuFilter`, from the passes that filter the texels; and the errors of reading the texture back, decoding its texels and encoding them again, writing the `-Format` named, and making the new texture that [Resize-WgpuTexture](Texture-Cmdlets.md#resize-wgputexture) lists. Each is described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md).'
        'ConvertTo-WgpuNormalMap' = '`WgpuNoTexture`; `WgpuNormalMap`, for a strength that is not finite, a format that would store the normals as sRGB colors, a `-TwoChannel` the format cannot lay out, the Min or Max mip filter, and a height map that is not 2D or is a cube map; and `WgpuMipFilter` and `WgpuMipEdge`, for mip settings that change nothing. From reading the height map back, `WgpuAspect`, `WgpuBuffer`, `WgpuTextureRead`, `WgpuSubmit`, `WgpuSubmitThread`, `WgpuPoll`, `WgpuRead`, `WgpuMap` and `WgpuStopped`; from making the normals, `WgpuTextureDecode`, `WgpuTransform`, `WgpuConvert` and `WgpuMipLevels`; from writing the format the normal map takes, `WgpuUnknownFormat`, `WgpuTextureFormat`, `WgpuCompress`, `WgpuCompressFormat`, `WgpuBasisEncode`, `WgpuKtx2` and `WgpuTextureFile`; and from making it, `WgpuTexture`, `WgpuTexelCount` and `WgpuTextureWrite`. Each is described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md).'
        'ConvertFrom-WgpuCubeMap' = '`WgpuNoTexture`; `WgpuCubeMap`, for a texture that is not six square layers, `-Layout` with `-Panorama`, `-Yaw` or `-FaceSize` with a layout of cells, a `-Yaw` that is not finite or a `-FaceSize` of 0, and from the pass that resamples a projection; `WgpuMipLevels`, for a `-MipLevel` past the cube''s last; and the errors of reading the cube back, converting its texels, writing the format the image takes and making it that [ConvertTo-WgpuCubeMap](Texture-Cmdlets.md#convertto-wgpucubemap) lists. Each is described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md).'
        'ConvertTo-WgpuCubeMap' = '`WgpuCubeMap`, for a count of textures other than one or six, six faces that differ in size or format or are not square 2D textures of one layer, an image of a shape no layout or projection has or that the `-Layout` named does not fit, `-Layout`, `-Yaw` or `-FaceSize` beside six faces or a layout of cells, a `-Yaw` that is not finite or a `-FaceSize` of 0, and from the passes that resample a projection. From reading the textures back, `WgpuTextureUsage`, `WgpuAspect`, `WgpuBuffer`, `WgpuTextureRead`, `WgpuSubmit`, `WgpuSubmitThread`, `WgpuPoll`, `WgpuRead`, `WgpuMap` and `WgpuStopped`; from decoding and converting their texels, `WgpuTextureDecode`, `WgpuConvert` and `WgpuMipLevels`; from writing the format the cube takes, `WgpuUnknownFormat`, `WgpuTextureFormat`, `WgpuTexels`, `WgpuCompress`, `WgpuCompressFormat`, `WgpuBasisEncode`, `WgpuKtx2` and `WgpuTextureFile`; and from making it, `WgpuTexture`, `WgpuTexelCount` and `WgpuTextureWrite`. Each is described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md).'
        'ConvertTo-WgpuIrradianceMap' = '`WgpuNoTexture`; `WgpuCubeMap`, for an environment that is neither six square layers nor one image a cube is read from, `-Layout` or `-Yaw` beside six faces, a `-FaceSize` of 0, and from its passes; and the errors of reading the environment back, reading a cube from one image, writing the format the map takes and making it that [ConvertTo-WgpuCubeMap](Texture-Cmdlets.md#convertto-wgpucubemap) lists. Each is described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md).'
        'ConvertTo-WgpuSpecularMap' = '`WgpuNoTexture`; `WgpuSamples`, for a `-Samples` of 0; `WgpuMipLevels`, for more `-MipLevels` than the faces have; `WgpuCubeMap`, for an environment that is neither six square layers nor one image a cube is read from, `-Layout` or `-Yaw` beside six faces, and from its passes; and the errors of reading the environment back, reading a cube from one image, writing the format the map takes and making it that [ConvertTo-WgpuCubeMap](Texture-Cmdlets.md#convertto-wgpucubemap) lists. Each is described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md).'
        'ConvertTo-WgpuShader' ='`WgpuNoShader`, `WgpuShaderFile`, `WgpuSpirV`, `WgpuStage`, `WgpuShaderInvalid`, `WgpuNoEntryPoint`, `WgpuEntryPointAmbiguous`, `WgpuOverrides`, `WgpuVersion`, `WgpuTranslate` and `WgpuOutFile`, each described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md).'
        'Copy-WgpuBuffer' = '`WgpuNoBuffer`, `WgpuRange`, `WgpuOtherDevice`, `WgpuCopyAlignment`, `WgpuCopy`, `WgpuSubmit`, `WgpuSubmitThread`, `WgpuPoll` and `WgpuStopped`, each described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md).'
        'Export-WgpuImage' = '`WgpuNoTexture`, `WgpuImage`, `WgpuImageExtension`, `WgpuImageFormat`, `WgpuUnknownFormat`, `WgpuQuality`, `WgpuEffort`, `WgpuDecoder`, `WgpuLayer`, `WgpuZstd`, `WgpuCube`, `WgpuImageShape` and `WgpuImageWrite`; with a new size or orientation, `WgpuResize`, `WgpuCrop`, `WgpuPad`, `WgpuRotate` and `WgpuTransform`; for `-Blur`, `-Sharpen` and their settings, `WgpuBlur`, `WgpuSharpen` and `WgpuFilterEdge`, and `WgpuFilter`, from the passes that filter the texels; for `-HeightToNormal`, the normal steps, `-NormalMips` and `-TwoChannel`, `WgpuNormalMap`; for `-Layout`, `-Panorama`, `-Yaw` and `-FaceSize`, `WgpuCubeMap`, which the passes that resample a projection raise too; from reading the texture back, `WgpuAspect`, `WgpuBuffer`, `WgpuTextureRead`, `WgpuSubmit`, `WgpuSubmitThread`, `WgpuPoll`, `WgpuRead`, `WgpuMap` and `WgpuStopped`; and from converting, decoding and encoding its texels, `WgpuTextureFormat`, `WgpuTextureDecode`, `WgpuConvert`, `WgpuMipLevels`, `WgpuCompress`, `WgpuCompressFormat`, `WgpuBasisEncode`, `WgpuKtx2` and `WgpuTextureFile`. Each is described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md).'
        'Get-WgpuAdapter' = '`WgpuLoader`, raised on Windows when psapi.dll or dbghelp.dll cannot be loaded and pinned before the first adapters are listed; described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md). Pinning them keeps NVIDIA''s driver from deadlocking a thread that loads them while another exits.'
        'Get-WgpuDevice' = 'Opening the default device: `WgpuLoader`, `WgpuNoAdapter` and `WgpuDevice`, each described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md).'
        'Get-WgpuShaderInfo' = '`WgpuNoShader`, `WgpuShaderFile`, `WgpuSpirV`, `WgpuStage` and `WgpuShaderInvalid`, each described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md).'
        'Get-WgpuTextureFormat' = 'Without `-Device`, opening the default device: `WgpuLoader`, `WgpuNoAdapter` and `WgpuDevice`, each described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md).'
        'Import-WgpuImage' = '`WgpuImage`, `WgpuSrgb`, `WgpuUnknownFormat`, `WgpuQuality`, `WgpuEffort`, `WgpuImageFormat`, `WgpuTextureFile` and `WgpuKtx2`; with a new size or orientation, `WgpuResize`, `WgpuCrop`, `WgpuPad`, `WgpuRotate` and `WgpuTransform`; for `-Blur`, `-Sharpen` and their settings, `WgpuBlur`, `WgpuSharpen` and `WgpuFilterEdge`, and `WgpuFilter`, from the passes that filter the texels; for `-HeightToNormal`, the normal steps, `-NormalMips` and `-TwoChannel`, `WgpuNormalMap`; for `-Cube`, `-Layout`, `-Yaw` and `-FaceSize`, `WgpuCubeMap`, which the passes that resample a projection raise too, and `WgpuCube`, for layers that are not square or not six to a cube; from converting, decoding and encoding its texels, `WgpuTextureFormat`, `WgpuTextureDecode`, `WgpuConvert`, `WgpuMipLevels`, `WgpuCompress`, `WgpuCompressFormat` and `WgpuBasisEncode`, and from the GPU work these take, `WgpuBuffer`, `WgpuTextureRead`, `WgpuSubmit`, `WgpuSubmitThread`, `WgpuPoll`, `WgpuRead`, `WgpuMap` and `WgpuStopped`; from making the texture, `WgpuTextureUsage`, `WgpuTexture`, `WgpuTexelCount` and `WgpuTextureWrite`; and without `-Device`, opening the default device: `WgpuLoader`, `WgpuNoAdapter` and `WgpuDevice`. Each is described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md).'
        'Invoke-WgpuCompute' = 'The shader: `WgpuNoShader`, `WgpuShaderInvalid`, `WgpuSpirV`, `WgpuNoEntryPoint`, `WgpuEntryPointAmbiguous`, `WgpuNotCompute`, `WgpuLayout`, `WgpuShader` and `WgpuPipeline`. The resources: `WgpuBindingCount`, `WgpuBindingKey`, `WgpuNoBinding`, `WgpuBindingMissing`, `WgpuNotStruct`, `WgpuNoMember`, `WgpuMemberNotNumbers`, `WgpuMemberSize`, `WgpuWrongResource`, `WgpuOtherDevice`, `WgpuEmpty`, `WgpuNoData`, `WgpuNotNumeric`, `WgpuOutOfRange`, `WgpuBuffer` and `WgpuBindGroup`. The run: `WgpuDispatchSize`, `WgpuNoDispatchSize`, `WgpuTooManyWorkgroups`, `WgpuImmediates`, `WgpuQuery`, `WgpuDispatch`, `WgpuSubmit`, `WgpuSubmitThread`, `WgpuPoll`, `WgpuRead`, `WgpuMap` and `WgpuStopped`. Without `-Device`, opening the default device: `WgpuLoader`, `WgpuNoAdapter` and `WgpuDevice`. Each is described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md), as is PWRS''s `PwrsConversionError` for a value that does not convert to a number.'
        'Invoke-WgpuMap' = 'The input: `WgpuNoData`, `WgpuNotNumeric`, `WgpuOutOfRange`, `WgpuVariableName`, `WgpuVariableLength`, `WgpuNoWgslType` and `WgpuNotFinite`. The expression: `WgpuShaderInvalid`, `WgpuMapUnused`, `WgpuLayout`, `WgpuShader` and `WgpuPipeline`. The run: `WgpuBuffer`, `WgpuBindGroup`, `WgpuDispatch`, `WgpuSubmit`, `WgpuSubmitThread`, `WgpuPoll`, `WgpuRead`, `WgpuMap` and `WgpuStopped`. Without `-Device`, opening the default device: `WgpuLoader`, `WgpuNoAdapter` and `WgpuDevice`. Each is described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md), as is PWRS''s `PwrsConversionError` for a value that does not convert to a number.'
        'Invoke-WgpuRender' = 'The target: `WgpuNoShader`, `WgpuNoTarget`, `WgpuUnknownFormat` and `WgpuTexture`. The shader: `WgpuShaderInvalid`, `WgpuNoEntryPoint`, `WgpuEntryPointAmbiguous`, `WgpuVertexInput`, `WgpuLayout`, `WgpuShader` and `WgpuRenderPipeline`. The pipeline''s tests and blend: `WgpuDepthFormat`, `WgpuTextureFormat`, `WgpuDepthTest`, `WgpuStencil`, `WgpuDepthBias` and `WgpuBlend`. The inputs: `WgpuNoVertices`, `WgpuVertexCount`, `WgpuNoData`, `WgpuNotNumeric`, `WgpuOutOfRange`, `WgpuBuffer`, `WgpuClearColor`, `WgpuClearDepth`, `WgpuClearStencil`, `WgpuBlendConstant`, `WgpuStencilReference`, and from `-Binding` the errors [Invoke-WgpuCompute](Compute-Cmdlets.md#invoke-wgpucompute) lists for resources. The draw: `WgpuDraw`, `WgpuSubmit`, `WgpuSubmitThread`, `WgpuPoll` and `WgpuStopped`. `-OutFile`: `WgpuImage`, `WgpuImageExtension`, `WgpuImageFormat`, `WgpuImageShape`, `WgpuImageWrite`, `WgpuTextureRead`, `WgpuRead` and `WgpuMap`. Without `-Device`, opening the default device: `WgpuLoader`, `WgpuNoAdapter` and `WgpuDevice`. Each is described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md).'
        'Join-WgpuTexture' = '`WgpuJoin` and `WgpuOtherDevice`; from reading the textures back, `WgpuTextureUsage`, `WgpuBuffer`, `WgpuTextureRead`, `WgpuSubmit`, `WgpuSubmitThread`, `WgpuPoll`, `WgpuRead`, `WgpuMap` and `WgpuStopped`; from decoding and resizing them, `WgpuTextureDecode`, `WgpuConvert` and `WgpuTransform`; from writing the format the new texture takes, `WgpuUnknownFormat`, `WgpuTextureFormat`, `WgpuCompress`, `WgpuCompressFormat`, `WgpuBasisEncode`, `WgpuKtx2` and `WgpuTextureFile`; and from making it, `WgpuTexture`, `WgpuTexelCount` and `WgpuTextureWrite`. Each is described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md).'
        'Measure-WgpuArray' = '`WgpuNoData`, `WgpuNotNumeric`, `WgpuOutOfRange`, `WgpuEmpty`, `WgpuNoWgslType`, `WgpuReduction`, and from running the reduction, `WgpuShader`, `WgpuPipeline`, `WgpuLayout`, `WgpuBuffer`, `WgpuBindGroup`, `WgpuDispatch`, `WgpuSubmit`, `WgpuSubmitThread`, `WgpuPoll`, `WgpuRead`, `WgpuMap` and `WgpuStopped`. Without `-Device`, opening the default device: `WgpuLoader`, `WgpuNoAdapter` and `WgpuDevice`. Each is described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md), as is PWRS''s `PwrsConversionError` for a value that does not convert to a number.'
        'Measure-WgpuTexture' = '`WgpuNoTexture`, and `WgpuMeasure`, for a `-Bins` of 0, a `-Range` that is not two finite numbers with the first below the second, and a histogram too large to hold in memory. From reading the texture back, `WgpuTextureUsage`, `WgpuAspect`, `WgpuBufferTooLarge`, `WgpuBuffer`, `WgpuTextureRead`, `WgpuSubmit`, `WgpuSubmitThread`, `WgpuPoll`, `WgpuRead`, `WgpuMap` and `WgpuStopped`; and from decoding its texels, `WgpuTextureDecode` and `WgpuTexels`. Each is described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md).'
        'New-WgpuBindGroup' ='`WgpuNoPipeline`, `WgpuNoGroup` and `WgpuBindGroup`; and from matching the resources to the bindings, `WgpuBindingCount`, `WgpuBindingKey`, `WgpuNoBinding`, `WgpuBindingMissing`, `WgpuNotStruct`, `WgpuNoMember`, `WgpuMemberNotNumbers`, `WgpuMemberSize`, `WgpuWrongResource`, `WgpuOtherDevice`, `WgpuEmpty`, `WgpuNoData`, `WgpuNotNumeric`, `WgpuOutOfRange` and `WgpuBuffer`. Each is described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md).'
        'New-WgpuBrdfTable' = '`WgpuBrdfTable`, for a `-Size` of 0; `WgpuSamples`, for a `-Samples` of 0; `WgpuCubeMap`, from its pass; from reading the table back, `WgpuBuffer`, `WgpuTextureRead`, `WgpuSubmit`, `WgpuSubmitThread`, `WgpuPoll`, `WgpuRead`, `WgpuMap` and `WgpuStopped`; from writing the format it takes, `WgpuUnknownFormat`, `WgpuTextureFormat`, `WgpuTexels`, `WgpuConvert`, `WgpuCompress`, `WgpuCompressFormat`, `WgpuBasisEncode`, `WgpuKtx2` and `WgpuTextureFile`; from making it, `WgpuTexture`, `WgpuTexelCount` and `WgpuTextureWrite`; and without `-Device`, opening the default device: `WgpuLoader`, `WgpuNoAdapter` and `WgpuDevice`. Each is described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md).'
        'New-WgpuBuffer' ='`WgpuNoData`, `WgpuNotNumeric`, `WgpuOutOfRange`, `WgpuEmpty`, `WgpuBufferTooLarge` and `WgpuBuffer`, and without `-Device` the errors of opening the default device, `WgpuLoader`, `WgpuNoAdapter` and `WgpuDevice`; each described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md). A value that does not convert to a number raises PWRS''s `PwrsConversionError`, described there too.'
        'New-WgpuCommandEncoder' = '`WgpuEncoder`, and without `-Device`, opening the default device: `WgpuLoader`, `WgpuNoAdapter` and `WgpuDevice`; each described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md). An encoder''s methods throw the errors [Wgpu.CommandEncoder](Types.md#wgpucommandencoder) lists.'
        'New-WgpuComputePipeline' = '`WgpuNoShader`, `WgpuShaderInvalid`, `WgpuSpirV`, `WgpuNoEntryPoint`, `WgpuEntryPointAmbiguous`, `WgpuNotCompute`, `WgpuLayout`, `WgpuShader` and `WgpuPipeline`, and without `-Device`, opening the default device: `WgpuLoader`, `WgpuNoAdapter` and `WgpuDevice`. Each is described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md), as is PWRS''s `PwrsConversionError` for a `-Constant` value that is not a number.'
        'New-WgpuQuerySet' = '`WgpuQuerySet`, raised also for a kind the device''s features do not cover, and without `-Device`, opening the default device: `WgpuLoader`, `WgpuNoAdapter` and `WgpuDevice`; each described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md). A query set''s methods throw the errors [Wgpu.QuerySet](Types.md#wgpuqueryset) lists.'
        'New-WgpuRenderPipeline' = '`WgpuNoShader`, `WgpuUnknownFormat`, `WgpuDepthFormat`, `WgpuTextureFormat`, `WgpuDepthTest`, `WgpuStencil`, `WgpuDepthBias`, `WgpuBlend`, `WgpuShaderInvalid`, `WgpuNoEntryPoint`, `WgpuEntryPointAmbiguous`, `WgpuVertexInput`, `WgpuLayout`, `WgpuShader` and `WgpuRenderPipeline`, and without `-Device`, opening the default device: `WgpuLoader`, `WgpuNoAdapter` and `WgpuDevice`. Each is described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md), as is PWRS''s `PwrsConversionError` for a `-Constant` value that is not a number.'
        'New-WgpuSampler' = '`WgpuSampler`, and without `-Device`, opening the default device: `WgpuLoader`, `WgpuNoAdapter` and `WgpuDevice`; each described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md).'
        'New-WgpuShader' = '`WgpuNoShader`, `WgpuShaderFile`, `WgpuSpirV`, `WgpuStage` and `WgpuShaderInvalid`, each described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md), as is PWRS''s `PwrsConversionError` for SPIR-V that is not numbers.'
        'New-WgpuTexture' = '`WgpuUnknownFormat` and `WgpuTexture`; with `-Data`, `WgpuNoData`, `WgpuNotNumeric`, `WgpuOutOfRange`, `WgpuAspect`, `WgpuTexelCount` and `WgpuTextureWrite`; and without `-Device`, opening the default device: `WgpuLoader`, `WgpuNoAdapter` and `WgpuDevice`. Each is described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md), as is PWRS''s `PwrsConversionError` for a value that does not convert to a number.'
        'Open-WgpuDevice' = '`WgpuTracePath`, `WgpuLoader`, `WgpuNoAdapter`, `WgpuUnknownFeature`, `WgpuFeatureUnsupported`, `WgpuFeatureExperimental` and `WgpuDevice`, each described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md).'
        'Read-WgpuBuffer' = '`WgpuNoBuffer`, `WgpuRange`, `WgpuRead`, `WgpuSubmitThread`, `WgpuPoll`, `WgpuMap` and `WgpuStopped`; `WgpuBufferTooLarge` for more elements than a .NET array holds; and with `-Destination`, `WgpuDestination`. Each is described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md).'
        'Read-WgpuTexture' = '`WgpuNoTexture`, `WgpuAspect`, `WgpuBuffer`, `WgpuTextureRead`, `WgpuSubmit`, `WgpuSubmitThread`, `WgpuPoll`, `WgpuRead`, `WgpuMap` and `WgpuStopped`, each described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md).'
        'Remove-WgpuBuffer' = '`WgpuNoBuffer`, described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md). A removed buffer''s later use fails with the error of that use, such as `WgpuRead`.'
        'Resize-WgpuTexture' = '`WgpuNoTexture`, `WgpuResize`, `WgpuCrop`, `WgpuPad` and `WgpuTransform`; `WgpuNormalMap`, for `-NormalMips` with the Min or Max filter; from reading the texture back, `WgpuAspect`, `WgpuBuffer`, `WgpuTextureRead`, `WgpuSubmit`, `WgpuSubmitThread`, `WgpuPoll`, `WgpuRead`, `WgpuMap` and `WgpuStopped`; from decoding its texels and encoding them again, `WgpuTextureDecode`, `WgpuConvert`, `WgpuMipLevels`, `WgpuCompress`, `WgpuBasisEncode`, `WgpuTextureFile` and `WgpuTextureFormat`; from writing the `-Format` named, `WgpuUnknownFormat`, `WgpuTexels`, `WgpuCompressFormat` and `WgpuKtx2`; and from making the new texture, `WgpuTexture`, `WgpuTexelCount` and `WgpuTextureWrite`. Each is described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md).'
        'Submit-WgpuCommand' = '`WgpuSubmitted`, `WgpuOtherDevice`, `WgpuSubmit`, `WgpuSubmitThread`, `WgpuPoll`, `WgpuStopped`, `WgpuDeviceLost` and `WgpuUncaptured`, each described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md).'
        'Test-WgpuShader' = '`WgpuNoShader`, `WgpuShaderFile`, `WgpuSpirV` and `WgpuStage`, each described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md). A shader that is not valid is no error: the cmdlet writes `$false`, or with `-Diagnostics` its problems.'
        'Wait-WgpuDevice' = 'Without `-Device`, opening the default device: `WgpuLoader`, `WgpuNoAdapter` and `WgpuDevice`. Waiting: `WgpuSubmitThread`, `WgpuPoll`, `WgpuStopped`, `WgpuDeviceLost` and `WgpuUncaptured`. Each is described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md).'
        'Write-WgpuBuffer' = '`WgpuNoData`, `WgpuNotNumeric`, `WgpuOutOfRange`, `WgpuRange` and `WgpuWrite`; and for a write that starts or ends inside a 4-byte word, which reads that word back first, `WgpuRead`, `WgpuSubmitThread`, `WgpuPoll`, `WgpuMap` and `WgpuStopped`. Each is described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md), as is PWRS''s `PwrsConversionError` for a value that does not convert to a number.'
        'Write-WgpuTexture' = '`WgpuNoTexture`, `WgpuNoData`, `WgpuNotNumeric`, `WgpuOutOfRange`, `WgpuAspect`, `WgpuTexelCount` and `WgpuTextureWrite`, each described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md), as is PWRS''s `PwrsConversionError` for a value that does not convert to a number.'
    }
    Classes = @{
        'Wgpu.Buffer' = '`Read`, `ReadAsync`, `ReadMemory` and `ReadMemoryAsync`, and a slice''s `Read` and `ReadAsync`: `WgpuRead`, `WgpuSubmitThread`, `WgpuPoll`, `WgpuMap` and `WgpuStopped`, and from those that return an array, `WgpuBufferTooLarge` for more elements than a .NET array holds. `ReadRange` and `ReadRangeAsync`: `WgpuRange` and those of `Read`. `ReadInto` and `ReadIntoAsync`, a buffer''s and a slice''s: `WgpuDestination`, `WgpuRead`, `WgpuSubmitThread`, `WgpuPoll`, `WgpuMap` and `WgpuStopped`. `Write` and `WriteAsync`: `WgpuNoData`, `WgpuNotNumeric`, `WgpuOutOfRange`, `WgpuRange` and `WgpuWrite`, and PWRS''s `PwrsConversionError` for a value that does not convert to a number; a write that starts or ends inside a 4-byte word reads that word back first, with the errors of `Read`. `Fill` and `FillAsync`: `WgpuOutOfRange` and `WgpuWrite`, PWRS''s `PwrsConversionError` for a value that does not convert to a number, and the errors of `Read` for a buffer whose bytes do not fill whole 4-byte words; a value of 0 clears the buffer, with the errors of `Clear`. `Clear` and `ClearAsync`: `WgpuClear`, `WgpuSubmit`, `WgpuSubmitThread`, `WgpuPoll` and `WgpuStopped`. `CopyTo` and `CopyToAsync`: `WgpuRange`, `WgpuOtherDevice`, `WgpuCopyAlignment`, `WgpuCopy`, `WgpuSubmit`, `WgpuSubmitThread`, `WgpuPoll` and `WgpuStopped`. `Slice`: `WgpuRange`. A method throws them as the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md) describes.'
        'Wgpu.CommandEncoder' = '`WgpuEncoderFinished`, `WgpuOtherDevice`, `WgpuAttachment` and `WgpuFinish`; and from `BeginRenderPass`, `WgpuClearColor`, and with a hashtable `WgpuRenderPassOption`, `WgpuClearDepth` and `WgpuClearStencil`. wgpu checks a pass''s commands when its encoder finishes, so an invalid command surfaces as `WgpuFinish`. A method throws them as the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md) describes.'
        'Wgpu.ComputePass' = '`WgpuPassEnded`, which a method throws as the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md) describes. wgpu checks the pass''s commands when its encoder finishes, so an invalid command surfaces there as `WgpuFinish`.'
        'Wgpu.RenderPass' = '`WgpuPassEnded`, and `WgpuIndexType` for an index buffer of neither UInt16 nor UInt32. A method throws them as the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md) describes. wgpu checks the pass''s commands when its encoder finishes, so an invalid command surfaces there as `WgpuFinish`.'
        'Wgpu.QuerySet' = 'Its reads: `WgpuRange`, `WgpuNotTimestamps`, `WgpuBuffer`, `WgpuQueryResolve`, `WgpuSubmit`, `WgpuSubmitThread`, `WgpuPoll`, `WgpuRead`, `WgpuMap` and `WgpuStopped`. A method throws them as the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md) describes.'
        'Wgpu.Device' = 'The constructor and `GetDefault`: `WgpuLoader`, `WgpuNoAdapter` and `WgpuDevice`. `Upload`: `WgpuNoData`, `WgpuNotNumeric`, `WgpuOutOfRange`, `WgpuEmpty`, `WgpuBufferTooLarge` and `WgpuBuffer`, and PWRS''s `PwrsConversionError` for a value that does not convert to a number. `Zeros` and `CreateBuffer`: `WgpuEmpty`, `WgpuBufferTooLarge` and `WgpuBuffer`. `CreateShader`: `WgpuSpirV`, `WgpuStage` and `WgpuShaderInvalid`. `CreateComputePipeline`: `WgpuShaderInvalid`, `WgpuNoEntryPoint`, `WgpuEntryPointAmbiguous`, `WgpuNotCompute`, `WgpuLayout`, `WgpuShader` and `WgpuPipeline`, and PWRS''s `PwrsConversionError` for a constant that is not a number. `CreateBindGroup`: `WgpuNoGroup`, `WgpuBindGroup` and the errors of matching resources to bindings that [New-WgpuBindGroup](Compute-Cmdlets.md#new-wgpubindgroup) lists. `CreateCommandEncoder`: `WgpuEncoder`. `CreateQuerySet`: `WgpuQuerySet`. `Submit` and `SubmitAsync`: `WgpuSubmitted`, `WgpuOtherDevice`, `WgpuSubmit`, `WgpuSubmitThread`, `WgpuPoll`, `WgpuStopped`, `WgpuDeviceLost` and `WgpuUncaptured`. `Wait` and `WaitAsync`: `WgpuSubmitThread`, `WgpuPoll`, `WgpuStopped`, `WgpuDeviceLost` and `WgpuUncaptured`. `Run` and `RunAsync`: the errors of binding and running that [Invoke-WgpuCompute](Compute-Cmdlets.md#invoke-wgpucompute) lists. `Download` and `DownloadAsync`: `WgpuRead`, `WgpuSubmitThread`, `WgpuPoll`, `WgpuMap` and `WgpuStopped`, and `WgpuBufferTooLarge` for more elements than a .NET array holds. `Destroy`: `WgpuPoll`. A method throws them as the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md) describes.'
        'Wgpu.ComputePipeline' = '`Dispatch` and `DispatchAsync` throw the errors of binding and running that [Invoke-WgpuCompute](Compute-Cmdlets.md#invoke-wgpucompute) lists. `BindGroup` throws `WgpuNoGroup`, `WgpuBindGroup` and the errors of matching resources to bindings that [New-WgpuBindGroup](Compute-Cmdlets.md#new-wgpubindgroup) lists. Each is described in the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md).'
        'Wgpu.Shader' = 'The constructor: `WgpuSpirV`, `WgpuStage` and `WgpuShaderInvalid`. `FromFile`: `WgpuShaderFile`, `WgpuSpirV`, `WgpuStage` and `WgpuShaderInvalid`. `FromSpirV`: `WgpuSpirV` and `WgpuShaderInvalid`, and PWRS''s `PwrsConversionError` for words that are not numbers. `ConvertTo`: `WgpuNoEntryPoint`, `WgpuEntryPointAmbiguous`, `WgpuOverrides`, `WgpuVersion` and `WgpuTranslate`. A method throws them as the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md) describes.'
        'Wgpu.Texture' = '`CreateView`: `WgpuUnknownFormat`, `WgpuViewDimension` and `WgpuTextureView`. `Read` and `ReadAsync`: `WgpuAspect`, `WgpuBuffer`, `WgpuTextureRead`, `WgpuSubmit`, `WgpuSubmitThread`, `WgpuPoll`, `WgpuRead`, `WgpuMap` and `WgpuStopped`. `Write`: `WgpuNoData`, `WgpuNotNumeric`, `WgpuOutOfRange`, `WgpuAspect`, `WgpuTexelCount` and `WgpuTextureWrite`. `Save` and `SaveAsync`: `WgpuImageExtension`, `WgpuImageFormat`, `WgpuDecoder`, `WgpuTextureDecode`, `WgpuConvert`, `WgpuImageShape`, `WgpuTextureFile`, `WgpuImageWrite` and the errors of reading the texture back. `GenerateMips` and `GenerateMipsAsync`: `WgpuMipLevels`, `WgpuTextureUsage`, `WgpuConvert`, `WgpuCompress` and `WgpuNormalMap`, the errors of reading the texture back, and from writing its levels or making the new texture, `WgpuTexture`, `WgpuTexelCount` and `WgpuTextureWrite`. `Compress` and `CompressAsync`: `WgpuUnknownFormat`, `WgpuCompressFormat`, `WgpuQuality`, `WgpuEffort`, `WgpuTextureFormat`, `WgpuConvert`, `WgpuCompress`, `WgpuBasisEncode`, `WgpuKtx2` and `WgpuTextureFile`, and the errors of reading the texture back and making the new one. `Resize`, `Crop`, `Pad`, `Flip`, `Rotate` and their Async forms: `WgpuResize`, `WgpuCrop`, `WgpuPad`, `WgpuRotate` and `WgpuTransform`, as [Resize-WgpuTexture](Texture-Cmdlets.md#resize-wgputexture) and [Convert-WgpuTexture](Texture-Cmdlets.md#convert-wgputexture) raise them for the same change, and the errors of reading the texture back, decoding its texels and encoding them again, and making the new texture that [Resize-WgpuTexture](Texture-Cmdlets.md#resize-wgputexture) lists. `Swizzle`, `Premultiply`, `Unpremultiply`, `ConvertColorSpace`, `AssignColorSpace`, `Grayscale`, `Invert`, `Adjust`, `ToneMap` and their Async forms: `WgpuSwizzle`, `WgpuColorSpace`, `WgpuGrayscale`, `WgpuAdjust` and `WgpuTransform`, as Convert-WgpuTexture raises them for the same change, and the same errors of reading, decoding, encoding and making. `ReconstructZ`, `Normalize`, `FlipGreen` and their Async forms: `WgpuNormalMap`, as Convert-WgpuTexture raises it for the same change, and the same errors of reading, decoding, encoding and making. `Blur`, `Sharpen`, `FindEdges` and their Async forms: `WgpuBlur`, `WgpuSharpen`, `WgpuEdges` and `WgpuFilter`, as Convert-WgpuTexture raises them for the same filter, and the same errors of reading, decoding, encoding and making. `ToNormalMap` and `ToNormalMapAsync`: the errors [ConvertTo-WgpuNormalMap](Texture-Cmdlets.md#convertto-wgpunormalmap) lists. `ToCubeMap`, `CubeFromFaces` and their Async forms: the errors [ConvertTo-WgpuCubeMap](Texture-Cmdlets.md#convertto-wgpucubemap) lists. `ToLayout`, `ToPanorama` and their Async forms: the errors [ConvertFrom-WgpuCubeMap](Texture-Cmdlets.md#convertfrom-wgpucubemap) lists. `ToIrradianceMap`, `ToSpecularMap` and their Async forms: the errors [ConvertTo-WgpuIrradianceMap](Texture-Cmdlets.md#convertto-wgpuirradiancemap) and [ConvertTo-WgpuSpecularMap](Texture-Cmdlets.md#convertto-wgpuspecularmap) list. `NewBrdfTable` and `NewBrdfTableAsync`: the errors [New-WgpuBrdfTable](Texture-Cmdlets.md#new-wgpubrdftable) lists. `Join`: the errors [Join-WgpuTexture](Texture-Cmdlets.md#join-wgputexture) lists. `Compare`, `Difference` and their Async forms: the errors [Compare-WgpuTexture](Texture-Cmdlets.md#compare-wgputexture) lists. `Measure` and `MeasureAsync`: the errors [Measure-WgpuTexture](Texture-Cmdlets.md#measure-wgputexture) lists, and PWRS''s `PwrsConversionError` for a range that is not numbers. A method throws them as the [Error Reference](Error-Reference.md) describes.'
    }
}
